      "refs": [
        "action:n2",
        "guard:b1->n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To begin the process in the Admin Office, first check if it has started."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly establishes the start (init), describes the initial check action (n2), implies the decision point (b1), and the guard captures the affirmative outcome allowing progression."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, verify the completeness of the invoices."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the second instructional step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If they are marked as \"Uncompleted\""
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional phrasing supports the decision gateway (b2) and its modeled-as-action predecessor (n5)."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "they should be returned to the client through postal mail."
      ],
      "justification": "The guard routes the positive/uncompleted branch, and the action exactly matches the prescribed return method."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if they are marked as \"Completed\", the process should be continued."
      ],
      "justification": "The negative/completed guard routes to the convergence point, which structurally represents the continuation of the process."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the invoices are returned to the client, receive the completed ones."
      ],
      "justification": "Faithfully captures the reception step following the return."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8",
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Then, mark the relevant box on the invoice entry form and proceed with checking if the process has been completed."
      ],
      "justification": "The span covers the marking action (n8), the subsequent check action (n9), and the implied decision point (b3)."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n10",
        "guard:b3->n11",
        "action:n10",
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, the process ends."
      ],
      "justification": "Both branch outcomes and their associated action/end nodes resolve to termination, faithfully reflecting the final instruction. Redundant terminal nodes are permissible."
    }
  ],
